RISC-V64: frameless frames (frame-pointer elision)

Adds frame-pointer elision for the riscv64 RyuJIT backend. Methods that do
not need a frame pointer (no localloc, no EH funclets, not varargs/OSR) are
emitted without saving/establishing FP, addressing locals off SP. Frees FP
(s0) as an allocatable callee-saved GPR.

Gated by the JitConfig knob RiscV64FramelessFrames (default 1 = enabled).
A second knob RiscV64ElideLeafRaSave (default 0 = disabled) exists for
leaf return-address elision but is currently off pending a fix.

Measured: ~2.2% fewer ZisK steps on a real Ethereum block, bit-identical
execution result.

